<p><strong>Addendum 2669.1 - Khevtuul 1 Survey Results</strong></p>
<p><em>Researcher's Note: The following is a representative sampling of exoplanets visited by SCP-2669. The attached information is a summary of findings; detailed records may be accessed with permission by the Office of Celestial Anomalies.</em></p>
<table class="wiki-content-table">
<tr>
<td colspan="3"><strong>Gliese 832 c</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th>Distance from Earth</th>
<th>Initial Heimdall HE Probability</th>
<th>Findings</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>16 light-years</td>
<td>17% probability of advanced civilization</td>
<td>No signs of current life; no evidence for previous inhabitation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan="3"><strong>Observational Notes:</strong> Unsurprising, given the initial chemical indicators that were in the mission file. The atmospheric readings have confirmed the presence of high amounts of oxygen, however, upon closer inspection, these appear to be related to other chemical processes occurring at the planet's surface. No electromagnetic signals or evidence of structures. But we weren't likely to strike gold on the first try anyway.</td>
</tr>
</table>
<table class="wiki-content-table">
