<th>Findings</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>560 light-years</td>
<td>33% probability of advanced civilization</td>
<td>No signs of current life; no evidence for previous inhabitation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan="3"><strong>Observational Notes:</strong> It's hard to say I am disappointed. I cannot understate the immense awe of being able to directly observe places that I never thought humans could reach. But given how similar in size to Earth this planet is, I was hoping to see more signs that, if life weren't present now, that it could have arisen at some point. No chemical indicators, even for bacteria, present. On to the next candidate.</td>
</tr>
</table>
<table class="wiki-content-table">
